From 3e7d784d1eb37367b2b3e7dc52882907fb5e529b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 04:10:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic_functions option: fixes of the review

- the out of bounds policy shared by the sources of a library of
  behaviours and the parameters handler of the material properties of the
  generic-parallel interface have a hidden visibility
  (`TFEL_VISIBILITY_LOCAL`): libraries of several backends loaded in the
  same process keep their own policies and parameters (no unique symbol
  of the process, checked by the tests);
- the header of the functions of the `generic` interface of a library of
  behaviours has its own name
  (`<name>-generic-parallel-<backend>-generic.hxx`), the `generic`
  interface being possibly used in the same call of MFront;
- `@GenerateMTestFileOnFailure` is treated by the interface: the functions
  of a point generate MTest files on failure as with `generic`;
- the configuration files of icpx request `-fp-model=precise` (errno set
  by the mathematical functions, strict floating point model);
- documentation: compilers translating host and device code in a single
  pass, `errno` with nvc++ (`-Mnobuiltin`), statistics read on the host by
  the report function, errors reported by asynchronous computations.
